# manual checks of clients until the account panel exists (TASK-ENG-036); sign in the panel first (Auth.http, the
# cookie dara.account), the https profile of the api; ids come from the answers; a client registers itself with a
# registration code (Auth.http), so there is no create here
@host = https://localhost:7105
@clientId = paste-a-client-id
@accessToken = paste-an-access-token

### every client of the account
GET {{host}}/account/clients

### one client of the account
GET {{host}}/account/clients/{{clientId}}

### the client reads itself: name (read-only there), type, context
GET {{host}}/clients/current
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### rename
PUT {{host}}/account/clients/{{clientId}}/name
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Bob-Phone-2" }

### the context of the client, added to prompts of its groups (never secrets)
PUT {{host}}/account/clients/{{clientId}}/context
Content-Type: application/json

{ "entries": { "Photos folder": "C:\\Users\\bob\\Pictures" } }

### revoke the client for good: no login code, refresh and access token refused, its hub connections closed
POST {{host}}/account/clients/{{clientId}}/revoke
